C/ABS 3D Printing Filament (p. 1, as the sheet states it)","certifications":null,"availability":null,"claim":null,"values":[{"key":"density","id":"V003377","value":1240,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"X-ECOMAX-CarbonX-CF-PC-ABS-TDS-v1-1","page":1,"twin":null,"at":"Density ISO 1183 g/cc"},{"key":"tensileModulusXY","id":"V003379","value":5.9,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"X-ECOMAX-CarbonX-CF-PC-ABS-TDS-v1-1","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture","treatment"],"at":"Tensile Modulus ISO 527 MPa"},{"key":"tensileStrengthXY","id":"V003378","value":62,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"X-ECOMAX-CarbonX-CF-PC-ABS-TDS-v1-1","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture","treatment"],"at":"Tensile Strength, Break ISO 527 MPa"},{"key":"elongationXY","id":"V003380","value":2,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"X-ECOMAX-CarbonX-CF-PC-ABS-TDS-v1-1","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture","treatment"],"at":"Tensile Elongation, Break ISO 527 %"},{"key":"flexuralModulusXY","id":"V003382","value":5.42,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"X-ECOMAX-CarbonX-CF-PC-ABS-TDS-v1-1","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture","treatment"],"at":"Flexural Modulus ISO 178 MPa"},{"key":"flexuralStrengthXY","id":"V003381","value":80,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"X-ECOMAX-CarbonX-CF-PC-ABS-TDS-v1-1","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture","treatment"],"at":"Flexural Strength ISO 178 MPa"},{"key":"hdt045","id":"V003384","value":130,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"X-ECOMAX-CarbonX-CF-PC-ABS-TDS-v1-1","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture","treatment"],"at":"Deflection Temperature at 0.45 ISO 75 °C"},{"key":"glassTransition","id":"V003383","value":137,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"X-ECOMAX-CarbonX-CF-PC-ABS-TDS-v1-1","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["moisture"],"at":"Glass Transition Temperature DSC °C"}],"listings":[],"held":[],"replaced":[],"print":{"nozzle":{"verdict":"within","state":"range","min":280,"max":300,"profileId":"P1399"},"bed":{"verdict":"within","state":"range","min":110,"max":120,"profileId":"P1399"},"chamber":{"verdict":"unknown","state":"unknown","min":null,"max":null,"profileId":"P0269"},"enclosure":null,"drying":{"need":"required","c":[null,110],"h":[null,4],"hoursOpen":false,"profileId":"P1399"},"hardened":true,"anneal":[],"advice":null,"from":{},"profileIds":["P0269","P1399"],"fromId":{}},"price":null,"notes":[{"topic":"Good for","items":[{"id":"Q06269","text":"CarbonX™ PC-ABS+CF has been formulated to offer improved thermal resistance and mechanical properties while retaining an ease of printability that makes it ideal for anyone seeking a structural component with high heat, high stiffness, excellent surface quality, and dimensional stability.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06286","text":"Ideal for any applications which require light weight and rigidity.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06287","text":"Carbon fiber reinforced parts, designed to use less material and save weight, is extremely popular in aerospace, civil engineering, the military, and motorsports.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Benefits","items":[{"id":"Q06267","text":"This material offers ease of printing, high thermal properties, strength & stiffness, excellent dimensional stability, and an amazing low-gloss surface finish.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06275","text":"Sturdy, rigid parts with durable qualities from PC and printability from ABS","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06276","text":"Easier to print than Polycarb, yet stiffer than ABS","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06277","text":"Greatly improved stiffness, modulus, and dimensional stability thanks to the addition of carbon fiber reinforcement","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Surface finish","items":[{"id":"Q06268","text":"an amazing low-gloss surface finish","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06278","text":"Beautiful low-gloss surface finish helps hide layer lines and makes highly technical-looking printed part","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"id":"Q06273","text":"Drying Specs 110°C for 4 hours","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06285","text":"Drying Instructions: 110°C for 4+ hours","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Nozzle wear","items":[{"id":"Q06271","text":"Nozzle Specs 0.4mm diameter minimum Hardened Steel Nozzle","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06280","text":"Nozzle: We strongly recommend a 0.4mm orifice or larger using one of our A2 Hardened Nozzles","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06288","text":"This material is particularly abrasive among 3D printing filaments.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06289","text":"Users may find standard brass nozzles are chewed through very quickly compared to standard wear and tear.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06290","text":"When worn through, the nozzle diameter will widen inconsistently and the printer will experience extrusion issues.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06291","text":"Because of this, it's strongly recommended this material be printed through a hardened steel nozzle rather than a softer metal.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Supports and removal","items":[{"id":"Q06274","text":"Supports Works best with X1 USM Water Soluble Support","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06284","text":"Supports: Water soluble AquaTek™ X1 USM works great for complex parts","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Printing advice","items":[{"id":"Q06270","text":"Heated Chamber Recommended","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06272","text":"Bed Adhesion Magigoo Bed Prep","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06279","text":"Bed Prep: Magigoo Bed Prep Adhesive gives us the best results","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06281","text":"Ideal layer height is 60% of nozzle diameter.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06282","text":"We do not recommend printing layers below 0.25mm with carbon fiber grades. Lower than 0.25mm may create too much back pressure in the hot end and result in poor feeding, jams, drive gear clicking, and eating a notch into the filament","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06283","text":"Heated Chamber: Recommended","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]}],"layers":[],"published":[],"environment":[],"guide":null,"resin":null,"sources":[{"id":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-9bf1f9fec020","publisher":"3DXTECH","title":"CarbonX PC-ABS+CF product page (archived 2023-06-03)","date":null,"read":"2026-10-04","kind":"Manufacturer product page or guide","url":"http://web.archive.org/web/20230603150315id_/https://www.3dxtech.com/product/carbonx-pc-abs-cf/","revision":"Internet Archive capture of 2023-06-03 15:03:15 UTC","note":"The 3DXTECH product page for CarbonX PC-ABS+CF as the Internet Archive captured it (the live address now redirects to the carbon-fibre collection). The registered TDS (v1.1) prints no print settings besides the test-bar conditions; this page prints the nozzle, bed, chamber, nozzle hardness and drying settings."},{"id":"X-ECOMAX-CarbonX-CF-PC-ABS-TDS-v1-1","publisher":"3DXTECH","title":"Technical Data Sheet: CarbonX™ Carbon Fiber PC/ABS 3D Printing Filament","date":null,"read":"2026-09-19","kind":"Manufacturer TDS","url":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0625/4185/6821/files/CarbonX_CF_PC_ABS_TDS_v1.1.pdf?v=1723942768"}]}